# A struct field on a recursive type cycle (a recursive edge) keeps an
# inline value (a struct or tuple) in a wrapper box the struct owns, and an
# enum or Option value as the pointer to its own counted box; the struct's
# drop releases either with the value. The program churns every cycle shape (list
# payload, Option, Map values, tuple, mutually recursive enums, edge-only
# struct, that struct captured by a closure, and an edge built from a
# constant) and panics when its peak RSS
# grows with the round count; the compile-time checksum runs the same shapes
# in the compiler (comptime tier).
# The web target is not Jet-hosted yet (E2104), so no web step.
fixture: cycle_struct_edges_free_with_their_struct.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
env: JETPACK_ENV=1
step: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
stdin: null
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = cycle_struct_edges_free_with_their_struct.stdout.expected
stderr: empty
step: jet run main.jet
stdin: null
limit: time=120
exit: 0
stdout: = cycle_struct_edges_free_with_their_struct.stdout.expected
stderr: empty
